  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best config so far is config_022 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat; acc=0.5353). RNA is the dominant signal (0.485 vs 0.208 for image-only), and the ViT-L image encoder provides a small but consistent boost over ResNet50. However, the multiprofile dimension (with its associated aggregation mechanism) is completely untested, representing the largest source of remaining uncertainty. Question: Does extending the best singleprofile multimodal setup to multiprofile with average-pool aggregation (config_024) improve over the singleprofile baseline (config_022)? This isolates the effect of multiprofile+avgpool while keeping the RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy fixed. Why this is the best next experiment: It tests the single most important unexplored architectural axis in the context of our strongest configuration. A positive result opens a rich sub-space (transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, other encoders) worth exploiting; a negative result efficiently prunes that entire branch. Using avgpool first (simpler, more interpretable) before transformer follows a logical exploration order, and the direct comparison to config_022 makes the result highly informative under a tight budget."
}

